WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.915
Most people buy a home with a mortgage.

00:00:03.115 --> 00:00:06.518
Here’s how it works in Ontario, and how Titled helps.

00:00:07.568 --> 00:00:09.172
First, the down payment.

00:00:09.371 --> 00:00:15.955
On a home you’ll live in, it’s 5% of the first $500,000, and 10% of the rest.

00:00:16.155 --> 00:00:19.950
On an $800,000 home, that’s $55,000.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.476
Next, the stress test.

00:00:22.676 --> 00:00:29.634
Lenders check you could still pay at your rate plus 2%, or 5.25%, whichever is higher.

00:00:30.684 --> 00:00:34.596
Put down less than 20%, and the mortgage must be insured.

00:00:34.796 --> 00:00:36.676
The premium is added to your loan.

00:00:36.876 --> 00:00:39.632
Land can’t be insured, so it needs more down.

00:00:40.682 --> 00:00:41.898
Buying with others?

00:00:42.099 --> 00:00:45.497
The lender adds up everyone’s income, debts and credit.

00:00:45.697 --> 00:00:49.424
And each borrower is usually responsible for the whole loan.

00:00:50.474 --> 00:00:55.126
When you’re ready, open a listing, tap “Finance it”, and ask our mortgage partner.

00:00:55.326 --> 00:01:00.919
A licensed agent compares banks, credit unions and private lenders, for any credit score.
